@startuml
title The three paths of traffic

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Browser" as B
component "Google front end\npublic address 203.0.113.20\nTLS, Cloud Armor" as GFE #ECEFF1
component "Web gateway pod\n10.20.x.x" as GW #E3F2FD
component "Service pod\n10.20.x.x" as S #E3F2FD
database "Cloud SQL\n10.40.0.3" as SQL #C8E6C9
component "Google APIs\n199.36.153.8/30" as API #ECEFF1
component "Cloud NAT\n203.0.113.10" as NAT #FFCDD2
component "Payment and e-mail\nproviders" as P

B --> GFE : 1. incoming\nHTTPS
GFE --> GW : straight to the pod
GW --> S : inside the cluster
S --> SQL : 2. private\nnever leaves the network
S --> API : 2. private access\nPub/Sub, secrets, telemetry
S --> NAT : 3. outgoing
NAT --> P : HTTPS, from one\nknown address
@enduml
